course: dictionary
lesson: 15336
title: Words that sound like what they mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound a bit like what they mean. Snuffling is one of them: say it out loud and you can almost hear a nose sniffing. Snuffling means breathing noisily through the nose.
explain: «Mia sat on the stairs, snuffling into a tissue because she had a cold.» The clues are the cold and the tissue. Snuffling is the noisy breathing of someone with a stuffy nose, or someone who is crying.
explain: The word also describes animals. «The hedgehog was snuffling in the hedge at night, looking for beetles.» Here snuffling means sniffing about noisily while searching for food. Check by swapping in your meaning: the hedgehog was sniffing about noisily, looking for beetles. It still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: «Snuffling» is the -ing form of the verb «snuffle».
fact: «Snuffling» means breathing noisily through the nose, as when you have a cold or are crying.
fact: «Snuffling» can also mean an animal sniffing about noisily, like a pig or hedgehog searching for food.
fact: As a noun, «snuffling» is the sound of this noisy breathing or sniffing.
fact: Clues for snuffling include a cold, tears, a tissue, or a creature sniffing around the ground.
exercise: «Mia sat on the stairs, snuffling into a tissue.» What is Mia doing? | Eating her lunch | Running up the stairs | *Breathing noisily through her nose | Singing a loud song
exercise: «The hedgehog was snuffling in the hedge at night, looking for beetles.» What is the hedgehog doing? | Singing to its friends | Sleeping quietly in a warm nest | *Sniffing about noisily, searching for food | Climbing up a tall tree
exercise: «The soft snuffling came from under the bed.» What does the word snuffling mean here? | A bright light shining | A soft blanket | A game played with friends | *The sound of noisy breathing or sniffing
test: «The puppy kept snuffling at the door, sniffing for the smell of its dinner.» What is the puppy doing? | Lying still and asleep | *Sniffing noisily about | Chewing a bone | Barking loudly
test: «Lily was crying quietly, and her snuffling could be heard across the room.» What does snuffling mean here? | Shouting for help | *Breathing noisily through her nose | Humming a tune | Laughing at a joke
exam: «The snuffling of the hedgehog woke Sam.» In this sentence, what kind of word is snuffling? | A question word | An adjective describing a person | A verb, an action happening now | *A noun, the sound itself
